					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-398957#post-1408899</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-398957/scp-929#post-1408899</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 03 Apr 2012 15:52:55 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Raikonos</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>223989</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>SCP-929 will always take the form of a younger member of the organisms species and will remain in this form until either the 'parent' organism is killed or hostilities are engaged against SCP-929.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p>After hostiles are killed or otherwise removed, SCP-929 will seek out a new 'parent' organism.</p> </blockquote> <p>What if the parent wasn't killed during the hostilities? Would SCP-929 still attach to a new one? If so, what happens to the old one?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
